/E (Braille is read by touch, so a plate that carries it needs raised dots with a clear shape. Mycelium composite copies the surface it grows against, and the way it touches the mold changes its colour and texture [1]. The mold surface can therefore act as a writing tool, and the open question is whether it can form dots that are solid and clear enough to read.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
