77 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 43 0 R
/T (Contact between the mold and the mycelium changes the colour and pattern of the skin, and in the first trials of Globa et al. a fully continuous contact stopped the skin from forming [1]. The skin develops where substrate meets air, with denser hyphae than the interior [4]. My domes sit against the lid, so I watch whether the skin forms there.)
/E (Contact between the mold and the mycelium changes the colour and pattern of the skin, and in the first trials of Globa et al. a fully continuous contact stopped the skin from forming [1]. The skin develops where substrate meets air, with denser hyphae than the interior [4]. My domes sit against the lid, so I watch whether the skin forms there.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
