/Title (Contact between the mold and the mycelium changes the colour and pattern of the skin, and in the first trials of Globa et al. a fully continuous contact stopped the skin from forming [1]. The skin develops where substrate meets air, with denser hyphae than the interior [4]. My domes sit against the lid, so I watch whether the skin forms there.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 335 0 R
/Prev 375 0 R
>>
